| `agent edit policy` | Refuses an agent edit to the judge (config/project.json `agents`), to a file git does not track, or outside the run's `--allow` files, and a spec that names a gate, before any write, so an agent cannot edit the checks, tests or config that decide whether its edit stays. | `python3 scripts/apply_refactor.py --spec - --allow <file>` | [`agents.protected_paths.<path>`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`agents.protected_names.<name>`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`agents.editable_names.<name>`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Not a sandbox: an interactive agent's direct edit outside `scripts/apply_refactor.py` is not refused, and a judge the project adds is protected only when listed. A durable `refactor.journal_path` transaction restores raw bytes and modes on red or startup after a pre-commit interruption; `RollbackError` retains the journal after failed restores. Recovery runs before the next spec, with paths in `recovered`; conflicts (`journal_conflict`) and lock contention (`lock_busy`) stop both agents. The gate waits for its process-group id to be durable before starting; recovery names a live group when refusing. A failed committed publication re-saves applied before restoration; committed startup cleanup logs to stderr. Restoration runs even if the applied re-save fails. `--recover` replays or cleans without reading a spec or stdin; human-only `--discard-journal --yes` abandons evidence without touching targets and refuses without confirmation. These modes and `--dry-run` are exclusive. Gate changes outside planned files are not restored. | [coding-practices.md](../guides/coding-practices.md) | always |
